.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-UPGRADE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-upgrade
.Nd upgrade the stack, Ollama, or an individual service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad upgrade
.Op Ar TARGET
.Op Fl -check
.Op Fl -force
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad upgrade
brings NOMAD components up to date.
With no
.Ar TARGET
it upgrades everything: the compose stack
.Pq admin, mysql, redis, dozzle, updater
and native Ollama, then prints guidance for upgrading admin-spawned services.
.Pp
A
.Ar TARGET
of
.Cm ollama
upgrades native Metal Ollama through Homebrew and restarts its LaunchAgent.
A
.Ar TARGET
of
.Cm admin ,
.Cm mysql ,
.Cm redis ,
.Cm dozzle ,
or
.Cm updater
upgrades that one compose service.
Any other
.Ar TARGET
.Pq for example Cm kiwix
is treated as an admin-spawned service and upgraded with its own
service-specific safety checks.
.Pp
While upgrading, the Mac is kept awake so multi-gigabyte pulls and Homebrew
bottle downloads are not interrupted by sleep.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -check
Dry run: report what would be upgraded and the current versions without
making any changes.
.It Fl -force
For a Kiwix upgrade, proceed even when the admin service cannot be queried
to confirm there are no in-progress ZIM downloads.
Use only when you accept the risk of restarting Kiwix mid-write.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad upgrade
Upgrade the full stack and native Ollama.
.It Ic nomad upgrade ollama
Upgrade native Ollama through Homebrew and restart it.
.It Ic nomad upgrade admin --check
Report whether the admin service has an update available, without applying it.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-services 1
